# Owlry web app — environment.
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. With these UNSET, the app runs entirely
# local (IndexedDB) exactly as it does today; setting them lights up the
# Supabase backend (XP / ink / coins / calendar / radar served from the server).
#
# The anon key is a PUBLIC key — safe to ship to the browser; Row-Level
# Security is what actually protects the data.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-PUBLIC-KEY

# ── the live owl chat + memory ─────────────────────────────────────
# The owl's brain runs in the `owl-chat` / `owl-peek` Supabase edge
# functions (Flash-Lite digests the ask + memory into a semantic query →
# Flash Scout picks the book → Flash Peek writes the letter on tap).
# The model key is a SERVER-SIDE Supabase secret — NEVER shipped to the
# browser:
#   supabase secrets set GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...
# then deploy:
#   supabase functions deploy owl-chat owl-peek signup-with-invite
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey.
# Models live in supabase/functions/_shared/gemini.ts
# (gemini-3.1-flash-lite for the digest/memory, gemini-3.5-flash for
# chat/letter).
#
# ⚠ FREE TIER TRAINS ON READER CONTENT. Google's free tier is marked
# "content used to improve our products: Yes" — on a free key, every
# reader's chat and stored memory (including anything the digest tags
# note_domain: crisis / addiction / grief / medical) becomes Google
# training data. The PAID tier is the inverse: content explicitly NOT
# used for training. The owl currently runs on the free tier by choice —
# revisit before real readers arrive, and note the free tier also caps
# the whole app at roughly 10 req/min and ~1,500 req/day ACROSS ALL
# USERS (a single chat turn spends 3 of those; a letter tap spends a
# 4th), well under the per-reader limits owl-chat itself allows.
#
# With a backend configured, the live owl answers by default. To force
# the offline mockup brain everywhere (e.g. for demos), set:
# VITE_OWL_LIVE=off
#
# (Users can also flip live ⇄ classic any time in Settings → THE OWL.)

# ── real book covers + metadata ────────────────────────────────────
# Real cover images + about-sheet metadata (subtitle, publisher, rating +
# ratings count, description) come from two sources, tried in order:
#   1. Google Books — richer (incl. descriptions), but its JSON API no longer
#      serves keyless requests (0/day anonymous quota), so it's used only when
#      a key is set below.
#   2. Open Library — free, keyless, CORS-enabled. The FALLBACK that makes
#      covers work for everyone with NO setup. This is why covers already work
#      out of the box; the catalog is pre-baked from it (npm run books:enrich).
#
# So the key below is OPTIONAL — it just upgrades primary lookups to Google's
# richer data. It's a PUBLIC, HTTP-referrer-restricted key (safe in the browser,
# like the Supabase anon key). Leave it unset and everything still works via
# Open Library.
#
# To add it (free): https://console.cloud.google.com → enable "Books API" →
# Credentials → Create API key → restrict to HTTP referrers app.owlry.ai/* and
# *.github.io/*, and to the Books API.
#
# VITE_GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY=YOUR-BOOKS-API-KEY
#
# Re-bake the 24 built-ins' covers into the bundle any time (uses the key if
# exported, else Open Library):
#   npm run books:enrich
#   GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY=your-key npm run books:enrich   # prefer Google
